{"type":"message","id":"4d4574a0","parentId":"08a1a2b4","timestamp":"2026-02-27T01:40:00.266Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_6b4f57qmj6d4_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"total 28\ndrwxrwxr-x 2 one one 4096 Feb 26 19:30 .\ndrwxrwxr-x 7 one one 4096 Feb 26 22:58 ..\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 one one 3038 Feb 27 08:39 fsrs.js\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 one one 2808 Feb 27 08:40 scheduler.js\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 one one 8503 Feb 27 08:39 storage.js"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":6,"aggregated":"total 28\ndrwxrwxr-x 2 one one 4096 Feb 26 19:30 .\ndrwxrwxr-x 7 one one 4096 Feb 26 22:58 ..\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 one one 3038 Feb 27 08:39 fsrs.js\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 one one 2808 Feb 27 08:40 scheduler.js\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 one one 8503 Feb 27 08:39 storage.js","cwd":"/home/one/.openclaw/agents/leader-agent"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1772156400263}}
{"type":"message","id":"df63bcbe","parentId":"4d4574a0","timestamp":"2026-02-27T01:40:02.709Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me read the fsrs.js to understand the FSRS algorithm.","thinkingSignature":"73021e916108ce8438a2e4e697095612d5535ea941632a8462a671448c547bed"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_qc6nra0sb3il_1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/one/.openclaw/skills/fsrs-memory/src/fsrs.js"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.5","usage":{"input":14132,"output":56,"cacheRead":7853,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22041,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772156400266}}
{"type":"message","id":"81b4aa63","parentId":"df63bcbe","timestamp":"2026-02-27T01:40:02.728Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_qc6nra0sb3il_1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// fsrs.js - Complete FSRS implementation using official fsrs.js library\nconst { FSRS, Card, Rating, State } = require('fsrs.js');\n\nconst fsrs = new FSRS();\n\nconst FSRSEngine = {\n  // Rating enum\n  Rating: {\n    Again: 1,\n    Hard: 2,\n    Good: 3,\n    Easy: 4\n  },\n  \n  // State enum\n  State: {\n    New: 0,\n    Learning: 1,\n    Review: 2,\n    Relearning: 3\n  },\n  \n  // Convert database card to FSRS Card object\n  dbToCard(dbCard) {\n    const card = new Card();\n    \n    // Set initial values\n    card.ease_factor = dbCard.ease_factor || 2.5;\n    card.reps = dbCard.repetitions || 0;\n    card.lapses = dbCard.lapses || 0;\n    \n    // Determine state\n    if (dbCard.state === 'new' || !dbCard.repetitions || dbCard.repetitions === 0) {\n      card.state = State.New;\n    } else if (dbCard.state === 'learning') {\n      card.state = State.Learning;\n    } else if (dbCard.state === 'relearning') {\n      card.state = State.Relearning;\n    } else {\n      card.state = State.Review;\n    }\n    \n    // Calculate interval from due_date if exists\n    if (dbCard.due_date) {\n      const dueDate = new Date(dbCard.due_date);\n      const now = new Date();\n      const intervalMs = dueDate - now;\n      card.interval = Math.max(0, intervalMs / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));\n    }\n    \n    return card;\n  },\n  \n  // Process a review and return scheduling info\n  repeat(card, ratingValue) {\n    const now = new Date();\n    \n    // Map rating 1-5 to FSRS Rating\n    let rating;\n    switch(ratingValue) {\n      case 1: rating = Rating.Again; break;\n      case 2: rating = Rating.Hard; break;\n      case 3: rating = Rating.Good; break;\n      case 4: rating = Rating.Easy; break;\n      case 5: rating = Rating.Easy; break; // Perfect maps to Easy with bonus\n      default: rating = Rating.Good;\n    }\n    \n    // Get scheduling result\n    const result = fsrs.repeat(card, now);\n    const scheduling = result[rating];\n    \n    if (!scheduling) {\n      console.error('Scheduling not found for rating:', rating);\n      return null;\n    }\n    \n    // Calculate interval in days\n    const dueDate = new Date(scheduling.card.due);\n    const intervalMs = dueDate - now;\n    const intervalDays = Math.max(0, intervalMs / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));\n    \n    // Map state to string\n    const stateMap = {\n      [State.New]: 'new',\n      [State.Learning]: 'learning',\n      [State.Review]: 'review',\n      [State.Relearning]: 'relearning'\n    };\n    \n    return {\n      due_date: scheduling.card.due.toISOString(),\n      interval: Math.round(intervalDays * 100) / 100,\n      ease_factor: scheduling.card.ease_factor,\n      repetitions: scheduling.card.reps,\n      lapses: scheduling.card.lapses,\n      state: stateMap[scheduling.card.state] || 'new',\n      stability: scheduling.card.stability,\n      difficulty: scheduling.card.difficulty\n    };\n  },\n  \n  // Calculate preview intervals without modifying card\n  previewIntervals(card, ratingValue) {\n    const fsrsCard = this.dbToCard(card);\n    return this.repeat(fsrsCard, ratingValue);\n  }\n};\n\nmodule.exports = FSRSEngine;\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1772156402726}}
{"type":"message","id":"3b849c02","parentId":"81b4aa63","timestamp":"2026-02-27T01:40:29.215Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the FSRS implementation better. Let me focus on the issue at hand. Looking at the code, I think I found the issue.\n\nIn the deck API, the server.js calculates `card_count` and `due_count`:\n\n```javascript\nconst decks = db.prepare(`\n  SELECT d.*, \n    (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM cards WHERE deck_id = d.id) as card_count,\n    (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM cards WHERE deck_id = d.id AND due_date <= datetime('now')) as due_count\n  FROM decks d \n  ORDER BY d.id ASC\n`).all();\n```\n\nThis looks correct. Let me trace through what happens:\n\n1. The deck shows 4 and 1 cards - that's the total count, which is correct\n2. But only 1 card shows in study view\n\nWait, let me re-read the issue description more carefully:\n\"网页上只，但两个牌组显示1张卡片分别显示包含4和1张卡片\"\n\nI think this is saying:\n- The webpage only shows 1 card (for studying)\n- But the two decks display 1 card each (as due) but actually contain 4 and 1 cards\n\nHmm, but the current data shows no cards are actually due. Let me check if the issue might be in how the due cards are being queried.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the problem statement:\n- \"网页上只，但两个牌组显示1张卡片分别显示包含4和1张卡片\"\n\nI think it's saying:\n- Webpage shows only 1 card (probably means the due card count is wrong - showing 1 when it should be different)\n- Two decks show 1 card each (but actually contain 4 and 1 cards total)\n\nWait, let me re-interpret this:\n- \"网页上只\" = The webpage only shows [something]\n- \"两个牌组显示1张卡片\" = Two decks show 1 card [each as due?]\n\n\n- \"分别显示包含4和1张卡片\" = [they] respectively show 4 and 1 cards [total]\n\nSo the deck list shows: deck 1 has 1 card due (but actually has 4 total), deck 2 has 1 card due (but actually has 1 total). The core issue appears to be that the due count for deck 1 is incorrect—it's displaying 1 when there should be more cards due, while the total counts (4 and 1) are accurate. Looking at the database query, I need to check how `due_count` is being calculated to see why it's not matching the actual due cards. The API is using the correct ISO timestamp format, so that should work. Let me check the fsrs.js code to see if there's a state mismatch. When `previewIntervals` runs, it converts the card to FSRS format, but there's a potential issue: the state values stored in the database are strings like `'2.0'` and `'review'`, while the code expects integers for the State enum (0, 1, 2, 3). This mismatch could be causing the query to fail to find the correct cards.","thinkingSignature":"5505b4d0fd19bf37c2beefdeddcd519aed615c483c55834cb1814f5654508120"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_rs6fag1much0_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/one/.openclaw/skills/fsrs-memory && node -e \"\nconst Database = require('better-sqlite3');\nconst db = new Database('./data/cards.db');\n\n// Get all cards with all fields\nconst cards = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM cards').all();\ncards.forEach(c => {\n  console.log('Card:', c.id, 'deck_id:', c.deck_id, 'state:', c.state, 'due_date:', c.due_date);\n});\n\n// Check deck counts\nconst decks = db.prepare(\\`\n  SELECT d.*, \n    (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM cards WHERE deck_id = d.id) as card_count,\n    (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM cards WHERE deck_id = d.id AND due_date <= datetime('now')) as due_count\n  FROM decks d \n  ORDER BY d.id ASC\n\\`).all();\n\nconsole.log('\\\\nDecks with counts:');\ndecks.forEach(d => {\n  console.log('Deck:', d.name, 'card_count:', d.card_count, 'due_count:', d.due_count);\n});\n\n// Check what the actual query returns\nconst now = new Date();\nconsole.log('\\\\nCurrent time:', now.toISOString());\nconsole.log('\\\\nDue cards query (using datetime(now)):');\nconst due1 = db.prepare(\\\"SELECT * FROM cards WHERE due_date <= datetime('now')\\\").all();\nconsole.log(due1.length, 'cards due');\n\nconsole.log('\\\\nDue cards query (using ISO string):');\nconst due2 = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM cards WHERE due_date <= ?').all(now.toISOString());\nconsole.log(due2.length, 'cards due');\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.5","usage":{"input":15026,"output":1014,"cacheRead":7853,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23893,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772156402728}}
