{"type":"message","id":"b544912d","parentId":"b257f59a","timestamp":"2026-02-27T01:40:49.123Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK so now I understand better. Currently no cards are due because:\n- Current time is 2026-02-27T01:40:29.260Z (which is 09:40 in Shanghai)\n- Card 4 has due_date 2026-02-27T15:09:03.623Z (which is 23:09 in Shanghai)\n\nSo card 4 is due today but not yet. That means:\n- All 5 cards have future due dates\n- 0 cards are currently due\n\nBut the problem statement says \"网页上只，但两个牌组显示1张卡片分别显示包含4和1张卡片\" - this means:\n- The webpage shows 1 card (probably means \"1 card due\")\n- But the decks show 4 and 1 cards (total cards)\n\nSo the issue might be that:\n1. The deck display is showing 1 card as \"due\" when actually none are due\n2. OR there was a time when some cards were due but now they're not\n\nWait, let me look more carefully at the issue. Looking at the original problem again:\n- \"网页上只\" - The webpage only shows [something]\n- \"两个牌组显示1张卡片\" - Two decks show 1 card\n- \"分别显示包含4和1张卡片\" - respectively display/include 4 and 1 cards\n\nI think this means:\n- The deck cards show 1 card as due for each deck\n- But the total cards are 4 and 1 respectively\n\nSo the due_count is showing incorrectly. Let me look at the server.js to see if there's an issue with how due_count is calculated.\n\nActually wait, in my test just now, due_count showed 0. So the current state shows 0 due. But maybe the issue is when there ARE due cards.\n\nLet me re-read the problem statement more carefully. The user said:\n- \"网页上只，但两个牌组显示1张卡片分别显示包含4和1张卡片（逻辑错误）\"\n\n\n- The UI displays 1 card as due when it should be showing the correct count. The due_count calculation in server.js uses `datetime('now')` which is in UTC, but the frontend displays times in Shanghai timezone. If cards were due earlier in Shanghai time but still in the future UTC, they'd appear as due on the frontend but not match the backend calculation.\n\nLooking at card 4 specifically - its due_date is 2026-02-27T15:09:03.623Z, which converts to 23:09:03 in Shanghai (UTC+8). Since the current time in Shanghai is 09:40, this card isn't actually due yet. But I should verify whether the database stores dates in UTC or Shanghai time, since that could explain why the counts don't align.","thinkingSignature":"e960d00c738051517d3d10d74b568b690d7d5b36343119ce13a68b8f783445bf"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_4sv9ezmc3try_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/one/.openclaw/skills/fsrs-memory && node -e \"\nconst Database = require('better-sqlite3');\nconst db = new Database('./data/cards.db');\n\n// Check timezone info\nconsole.log('SQLite version:');\nconst version = db.prepare('SELECT sqlite_version() as version').get();\nconsole.log(version);\n\n// Try different timezone queries\nconsole.log('\\\\ndatetime(\\\"now\\\"):', db.prepare('SELECT datetime(\\\"now\\\") as now').get());\nconsole.log('datetime(\\\"now\\\", \\\"localtime\\\"):', db.prepare('SELECT datetime(\\\"now\\\", \\\"localtime\\\") as now').get());\nconsole.log('datetime(\\\"now\\\", \\\"+8 hours\\\"):', db.prepare('SELECT datetime(\\\"now\\\", \\\"+8 hours\\\") as now').get());\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.5","usage":{"input":16302,"output":779,"cacheRead":7853,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":24934,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772156429267}}
