{"type":"message","id":"6e25573b","parentId":"c2e7afdc","timestamp":"2026-02-27T01:41:07.567Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There's the bug! The SQLite `datetime('now')` returns UTC time (2026-02-27 01:40:52), while `datetime('now', 'localtime')` returns local time (2026-02-27 09:40:52 in Shanghai).\n\nThe server.js is using `datetime('now')` which compares against UTC, but all the due_date values in the database seem to be stored in a way that doesn't match.\n\nActually, wait. Let me check more carefully. The due dates are stored as ISO strings with 'Z' suffix (UTC), so comparing against UTC should work. Let me trace through what's happening:\n\n1. The due_date in DB: `2026-02-27T15:09:03.623Z` (UTC)\n2. `datetime('now')` returns: `2026-02-27 01:40:52` (UTC)\n3. Comparison: `2026-02-27 01:40:52` >= `2026-02-27T15:09:03.623Z` = false (card NOT due)\n\nSo actually, using `datetime('now')` should work correctly for comparing UTC timestamps!\n\nLet me check if the issue is something else. Let me also look at whether there might be an issue with the data state field. Looking at the card data:\n- Card 1: state = \"2.0\" (a number stored as string!)\n- Card 2: state = \"review\"\n- Card 3: state = \"2.0\"\n- Card 4: state = \"review\"\n- Card 7: state = \"review\"\n\nThe state values are inconsistent. Some are \"2.0\" (string), some are \"review\" (string). This could be a problem.\n\nBut wait, the main issue reported is:\n- Only 1 card shows in the study view\n- But decks show 4 and 1 cards\n\nSo the deck stats show total cards correctly (4 and 1), but the study view only shows 1 card. \n\nLooking at the loadDueCards function, it calls `/api/cards/due` with an optional deck parameter. I need to check if that endpoint is properly filtering by deck and returning the correct due cards.","thinkingSignature":"a6144ecf4ce1b8fd1e8f97845a22fa05d6e4387bbbd749f3e144575fb352dd47"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_fg8yekfy506e_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/one/.openclaw/skills/fsrs-memory/web && node -e \"\nconst Database = require('better-sqlite3');\nconst db = new Database('../data/cards.db');\n\n// Let's check the current state of things\nconst now = new Date();\nconsole.log('Current time (ISO):', now.toISOString());\n\n// Check due cards in different ways\nconsole.log('\\\\n1. Using datetime(now):');\nconst due1 = db.prepare(\\\"SELECT id, due_date FROM cards WHERE due_date <= datetime('now')\\\").all();\nconsole.log(due1);\n\nconsole.log('\\\\n2. Using ISO string:');\nconst due2 = db.prepare('SELECT id, due_date FROM cards WHERE due_date <= ?').all(now.toISOString());\nconsole.log(due2);\n\nconsole.log('\\\\n3. Using datetime with localtime:');\nconst due3 = db.prepare(\\\"SELECT id, due_date FROM cards WHERE due_date <= datetime('now', 'localtime')\\\").all();\nconsole.log(due3);\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.5","usage":{"input":17554,"output":711,"cacheRead":7853,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":26118,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772156452681}}
