{"type":"message","id":"8685153b","parentId":"95be0510","timestamp":"2026-02-27T01:47:41.237Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_31s98tmkhdod_1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// fsrs.js - Complete FSRS implementation using official fsrs.js library\nconst { FSRS, Card, Rating, State } = require('fsrs.js');\n\nconst fsrs = new FSRS();\n\nconst FSRSEngine = {\n  // Rating enum\n  Rating: {\n    Again: 1,\n    Hard: 2,\n    Good: 3,\n    Easy: 4\n  },\n  \n  // State enum\n  State: {\n    New: 0,\n    Learning: 1,\n    Review: 2,\n    Relearning: 3\n  },\n  \n  // Normalize state value to standard string\n  normalizeState(dbState, repetitions) {\n    // Handle undefined, null, or empty states\n    if (!dbState || dbState === '') {\n      return 'new';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle numeric states (convert to string)\n    const stateStr = String(dbState).trim();\n    \n    // Handle \"2.0\" or \"2\" which means Review\n    if (stateStr === '2.0' || stateStr === '2') {\n      return 'review';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle \"1.0\" or \"1\" which means Learning  \n    if (stateStr === '1.0' || stateStr === '1') {\n      return 'learning';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle \"3.0\" or \"3\" which means Relearning\n    if (stateStr === '3.0' || stateStr === '3') {\n      return 'relearning';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle \"0\" or \"0.0\" which means New\n    if (stateStr === '0' || stateStr === '0.0') {\n      return 'new';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle string states\n    const validStates = ['new', 'learning', 'review', 'relearning'];\n    if (validStates.includes(stateStr.toLowerCase())) {\n      return stateStr.toLowerCase();\n    }\n    \n    // Default: if repetitions is 0, treat as new\n    if (!repetitions || repetitions === 0) {\n      return 'new';\n    }\n    \n    // Otherwise treat as review\n    return 'review';\n  },\n  \n  // Convert database card to FSRS Card object\n  dbToCard(dbCard) {\n    const card = new Card();\n    \n    // Set initial values with defaults\n    card.ease_factor = dbCard.ease_factor || 2.5;\n    card.reps = dbCard.repetitions || 0;\n    card.lapses = dbCard.lapses || 0;\n    \n    // Normalize state before mapping\n    const normalizedState = this.normalizeState(dbCard.state, dbCard.repetitions);\n    \n    // Map normalized state to FSRS State\n    switch (normalizedState) {\n      case 'new':\n        card.state = State.New;\n        break;\n      case 'learning':\n        card.state = State.Learning;\n        break;\n      case 'relearning':\n        card.state = State.Relearning;\n        break;\n      case 'review':\n      default:\n        card.state = State.Review;\n        break;\n    }\n    \n    // Calculate interval from due_date if exists\n    if (dbCard.due_date) {\n      const dueDate = new Date(dbCard.due_date);\n      const now = new Date();\n      const intervalMs = dueDate - now;\n      card.interval = Math.max(0, intervalMs / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));\n    }\n    \n    return card;\n  },\n  \n  // Process a review and return scheduling info\n  repeat(card, ratingValue) {\n    const now = new Date();\n    \n    // Map rating 1-5 to FSRS Rating\n    let rating;\n    switch(ratingValue) {\n      case 1: rating = Rating.Again; break;\n      case 2: rating = Rating.Hard; break;\n      case 3: rating = Rating.Good; break;\n      case 4: rating = Rating.Easy; break;\n      case 5: rating = Rating.Easy; break; // Perfect maps to Easy with bonus\n      default: rating = Rating.Good;\n    }\n    \n    // Get scheduling result\n    const result = fsrs.repeat(card, now);\n    const scheduling = result[rating];\n    \n    if (!scheduling) {\n      console.error('Scheduling not found for rating:', rating);\n      return null;\n    }\n    \n    // Calculate interval in days\n    const dueDate = new Date(scheduling.card.due);\n    const intervalMs = dueDate - now;\n    const intervalDays = Math.max(0, intervalMs / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));\n    \n    // Map state to string\n    const stateMap = {\n      [State.New]: 'new',\n      [State.Learning]: 'learning',\n      [State.Review]: 'review',\n      [State.Relearning]: 'relearning'\n    };\n    \n    return {\n      due_date: scheduling.card.due.toISOString(),\n      interval: Math.round(intervalDays * 100) / 100,\n      ease_factor: scheduling.card.ease_factor,\n      repetitions: scheduling.card.reps,\n      lapses: scheduling.card.lapses,\n      state: stateMap[scheduling.card.state] || 'new',\n      stability: scheduling.card.stability,\n      difficulty: scheduling.card.difficulty\n    };\n  },\n  \n  // Calculate preview intervals without modifying card\n  previewIntervals(card, ratingValue) {\n    const fsrsCard = this.dbToCard(card);\n    return this.repeat(fsrsCard, ratingValue);\n  }\n};\n\nmodule.exports = FSRSEngine;\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1772156861233}}
{"type":"message","id":"efec65ed","parentId":"8685153b","timestamp":"2026-02-27T01:48:18.314Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait, I see the issue now! Looking at the library code:\n\n```javascript\n_proto2.repeat = function repeat(card, now) {\n```\n\nThe library expects `repeat(card, now)` where `now` is the second argument, but I see that in my code, I'm already calling `fsrs.repeat(card, now)` correctly. Let me check what's happening in the dbToCard function.\n\nActually, looking more closely at the error: `now.getTime is not a function` - this suggests that `now` is not a Date object. But I'm passing `new Date()` which should work.\n\nWait, I think I see the issue now! In the dbToCard function, I'm setting `card.interval` directly, but I'm not setting `card.due` correctly. Also, I'm not setting `card.last_review`. Let me fix this.","thinkingSignature":"efe645666f34d6b108fcf7a7492f006e3e4a12410d30b3999a3b884f3655d446"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_7de926i6jpx1_1","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"// fsrs.js - Complete FSRS implementation using official fsrs.js library\nconst { FSRS, Card, Rating, State } = require('fsrs.js');\n\nconst fsrs = new FSRS();\n\nconst FSRSEngine = {\n  // Rating enum\n  Rating: {\n    Again: 1,\n    Hard: 2,\n    Good: 3,\n    Easy: 4\n  },\n  \n  // State enum\n  State: {\n    New: 0,\n    Learning: 1,\n    Review: 2,\n    Relearning: 3\n  },\n  \n  // Normalize state value to standard string\n  normalizeState(dbState, repetitions) {\n    // Handle undefined, null, or empty states\n    if (!dbState || dbState === '') {\n      return 'new';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle numeric states (convert to string)\n    const stateStr = String(dbState).trim();\n    \n    // Handle \"2.0\" or \"2\" which means Review\n    if (stateStr === '2.0' || stateStr === '2') {\n      return 'review';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle \"1.0\" or \"1\" which means Learning  \n    if (stateStr === '1.0' || stateStr === '1') {\n      return 'learning';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle \"3.0\" or \"3\" which means Relearning\n    if (stateStr === '3.0' || stateStr === '3') {\n      return 'relearning';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle \"0\" or \"0.0\" which means New\n    if (stateStr === '0' || stateStr === '0.0') {\n      return 'new';\n    }\n    \n    // Handle string states\n    const validStates = ['new', 'learning', 'review', 'relearning'];\n    if (validStates.includes(stateStr.toLowerCase())) {\n      return stateStr.toLowerCase();\n    }\n    \n    // Default: if repetitions is 0, treat as new\n    if (!repetitions || repetitions === 0) {\n      return 'new';\n    }\n    \n    // Otherwise treat as review\n    return 'review';\n  },\n  \n  // Convert database card to FSRS Card object\n  dbToCard(dbCard) {\n    const card = new Card();\n    const now = new Date();\n    \n    // Set initial values with defaults\n    card.ease_factor = dbCard.ease_factor || 2.5;\n    card.reps = dbCard.repetitions || 0;\n    card.lapses = dbCard.lapses || 0;\n    card.difficulty = dbCard.ease_factor || 2.5;\n    card.stability = 0;\n    \n    // Normalize state before mapping\n    const normalizedState = this.normalizeState(dbCard.state, dbCard.repetitions);\n    \n    // Map normalized state to FSRS State\n    switch (normalizedState) {\n      case 'new':\n        card.state = State.New;\n        card.due = now; // New cards are due immediately\n        break;\n      case 'learning':\n        card.state = State.Learning;\n        card.due = new Date(dbCard.due_date) || now;\n        break;\n      case 'relearning':\n        card.state = State.Relearning;\n        card.due = new Date(dbCard.due_date) || now;\n        break;\n      case 'review':\n      default:\n        card.state = State.Review;\n        // For review cards, set due date properly\n        if (dbCard.due_date) {\n          card.due = new Date(dbCard.due_date);\n        } else {\n          card.due = now;\n        }\n        break;\n    }\n    \n    // Calculate elapsed_days from due_date if the card is review\n    if (dbCard.due_date && card.state === State.Review) {\n      const dueDate = new Date(dbCard.due_date);\n      card.elapsed_days = Math.max(0, (now - dueDate) / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));\n    } else {\n      card.elapsed_days = 0;\n    }\n    \n    // Set last_review if available\n    if (dbCard.last_review) {\n      card.last_review = new Date(dbCard.last_review);\n    } else {\n      card.last_review = now;\n    }\n    \n    return card;\n  },\n  \n  // Process a review and return scheduling info\n  repeat(card, ratingValue) {\n    const now = new Date();\n    \n    // Map rating 1-5 to FSRS Rating\n    let rating;\n    switch(ratingValue) {\n      case 1: rating = Rating.Again; break;\n      case 2: rating = Rating.Hard; break;\n      case 3: rating = Rating.Good; break;\n      case 4: rating = Rating.Easy; break;\n      case 5: rating = Rating.Easy; break; // Perfect maps to Easy with bonus\n      default: rating = Rating.Good;\n    }\n    \n    // Get scheduling result - pass card first, then now\n    const result = fsrs.repeat(card, now);\n    const scheduling = result[rating];\n    \n    if (!scheduling) {\n      console.error('Scheduling not found for rating:', rating);\n      return null;\n    }\n    \n    // Calculate interval in days from now to the scheduled due date\n    const dueDate = new Date(scheduling.card.due);\n    const intervalMs = dueDate - now;\n    const intervalDays = Math.max(0, intervalMs / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));\n    \n    // Map state to string\n    const stateMap = {\n      [State.New]: 'new',\n      [State.Learning]: 'learning',\n      [State.Review]: 'review',\n      [State.Relearning]: 'relearning'\n    };\n    \n    return {\n      due_date: scheduling.card.due.toISOString(),\n      interval: Math.round(intervalDays * 100) / 100,\n      ease_factor: scheduling.card.ease_factor,\n      repetitions: scheduling.card.reps,\n      lapses: scheduling