{"type":"message","id":"8440ff5f","parentId":"0ca1cebe","timestamp":"2026-02-27T01:51:11.247Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see the issue! The problem is that when inserting cards, the server uses `now.toISOString()` which produces UTC timestamps, but the queries use `datetime('now', 'localtime')` which compares against local time. \n\nThis creates a mismatch:\n- When a card is created: due_date is stored as UTC (e.g., \"2026-02-27T01:51:03.398Z\")\n- When querying due cards: we compare against localtime (e.g., \"2026-02-27 09:51:03\")\n\nThe UTC timestamp \"2026-02-27T01:51:03.398Z\" is equivalent to \"2026-02-27 09:51:03\" in Shanghai time, but SQLite's string comparison might not handle this correctly.\n\nActually wait, looking at the test, it works when I use `datetime('now', 'localtime')` to insert! But the server.js uses `now.toISOString()` to insert.\n\nThe fix should be to either:\n1. Use localtime when inserting cards too\n2. Or always use UTC for everything\n\nLet me fix the server to use localtime consistently.","thinkingSignature":"d40f97cf76870b9fef076b23d6f84708d596a084a338abfb2f6b554da2e7dd51"},{"type":"text","text":"我发现了一个问题 - 插入卡片时使用的是 UTC 时间，但查询时使用的是本地时间。让我修复这个问题：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_5ys5izooz6hl_1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/one/.openclaw/skills/fsrs-memory/web/server.js","limit":20,"offset":220}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.5","usage":{"input":54098,"output":328,"cacheRead":7853,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":62279,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772157063420}}
